 "protocol": {
  "summary": "Relaxed standing, sitting, lying supine, prone and lateral; loads measured a few days before anterior interbody fusion; video-synchronised telemetry.",
  "how_to_simulate": [
   "Model the patient (Table 1) in each body position: standing, sitting (stool), lying supine, prone, lateral",
   "No external load; relaxed posture",
   "Output the sagittal bending moment Mb,sag in the fixator rods (negative = flexion) or the trend of the flexion moment at the bridged level",
   "A whole-spine MSK model outputs total segment loads, not the fixator share; fixator loads depend strongly on surgical procedure (distraction/compression, bridged level, interbody fusion) - compare only trends/relative values unless the model includes the bisegmental fixator and its load sharing; robust targets: flexion moment upright >> lying, lateral > supine, sitting <= standing"
  ],
