   "disc_area_mm2": null
  },
  "notes": "Paired telemeterised bisegmental internal spinal fixators (modified Dick fixator), 3 force + 3 moment components per side; sign convention: negative axial force = fixator compression, negative Mb,sag = flexion bending moment. Anterior interbody fusion (AIF) with iliac-crest graft performed in a second operation (patients 3,5,7,9,10: only upper bridged disc removed). Median implant load values per body position determined over three measuring sessions at each time point (a few days before AIF; ~100 days after AIF, when wound pain had gone and solid fusion not yet occurred). Table headings say \"average implant loads\". Considerable left/right differences; in some cases flexion moment on one side and extension on the other. Patient 7: AIF preceded fixator implantation, so no pre-AIF data; patient 9 could not lie prone before AIF. Patient 8 had an additional anterior Zielke fixator after AIF. Text: highest axial forces for standing; flexion moments significantly lower lying than upright (P<0.001); loads not higher sitting than standing; flexion moment higher lateral than supine; slightly higher flexion moments after than before AIF (significance table = Table 4)."
 },
